{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1545052-range-bands-and-movement-am-i-missing-something","id":1545052,"title":"Range Bands and movement: am I missing something?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-30T08:31:52-07:00","id":1545052,"title":"Range Bands and movement: am I missing something?","content":"I can find this topic for exalted but not specifically for chronicles. In the Hurt Locker book we are given some new weapon rules. These make the process for abstract without having to keep track of individual bullets and overall I like that.<br /> <br /> it also modified the range system, giving us range bands that the firearms interact with. While I am on board with making things as simple as possible, being loathe to actually use my brain and think when other options are available, I am having a very hard time wrapping my head around how this is supposed to work.<br /> <br /> My main point of confusion is movement. Moving from one range band to another. As the book states, each successive band takes more \u201cmovement actions\u201d to get through. 1 from close to short, 2 for short to medium and so on. An additional table is provided if an ST wants a higher speed score to affect this travel time.<br /> <br /> My issue however is that I can\u2019t make sense of how this works in practice. I assume my mind is stuck on some minor detail or there is some piece of information I am missing. This method of movement doesn\u2019t seem to make any sense or work at all no matter how many times I read it.<br /> <br /> Primarily my issue is that distance is relative. Two objects are far away from each other, but near other things. If my frame of reference is my character, then something that is far away from me initially gets closer if I move towards it. <br /> <br /> so okay, I have an objective a short distance away from me and an opponent a medium distance away from me. It takes me 1 movement to get from Close to Short. Now the shirt is close and where I was is now short. All well and good. But does the medium distance change to become short now? Judging by the table it shouldn\u2019t. It takes 2 movement actions to cover the distance from short to medium. I would need to move and then use my action to move again and I reach it. But I should have already moved closer to it the first time when I moved to the short objective.<br /> <br /> If the medium distance becomes short, then I\u2019m not moving from short to medium, I\u2019m still moving from close to short. If it doesn\u2019t change, then how did I not end up moving closer to it when I moved the first time? It doesn\u2019t make any sense to me. <br /> <br /> the only solution I can think of is that the point of reference has to be something outside the character. Some objective outside thing is designated as the starting point and everything is close, short, medium etc from that point. So radiating from that point you have progressively bigger bands (hence explaining why it takes more actions to cover them).<br /> <br /> I would simply assume that is the answer if it wasn\u2019t for the book stating the reference is generally the character\u2019s perspective.<br /> <br /> So help me out, am I missing something? Am I stupid? Or is the section actually supposed to work a different way but says otherwise?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-30T12:31:54-07:00","id":1545062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Jub-Jub</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1545052-range-bands-and-movement-am-i-missing-something#post1545052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So help me out, am I missing something? Am I stupid? Or is the section actually supposed to work a different way but says otherwise?</div> </div> </div> </div>The bands as described on the same page are progressively bigger stretches of distance regardless of where the frame of reference starts. If you're moving from Medium range to Close range, you've closed a distance of at least thirty meters if not a hundred; if you're moving from Short to Close you're moving less than thirty meters.<br /> <br /> &quot;Movement actions&quot; concern movement in a single turn \u2014 hence why Range and Movement references total number of movement actions in terms of maneuvers that fit into a single person's Initiative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-30T14:13:38-07:00","id":1545069,"title":"","content":"I posted the question elsewhere and someone helped me figure it out in a way I understood.<br /> <br /> basically I was thinking backwards. If I have an opponent at the medium range band, I am not moving into short and then medium, I am moving from medium to short. If they go before me and only use one movement action, then it gets to my turn and I use 1, 2 movement actions have occurred moving me from medium to short, I can then use my action to close the distance and move from short to close.<br /> <br /> i still have some confusion about weapon range, but I\u2019ll save embarrassing myself for another time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}